
# --- GOLDEN FIXTURE (see docs/guests/debian22.md) ---
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_RESET_MONITOR=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/debian22/reset-hmp.sock
SH_FIXTURE_DESC="Debian GNU/Linux 2.2 potato: XFree86 3.3.6 XF86_SVGA on Cirrus GD5446 at 1024x768x16, logged in as gallery on the GNOME 1.0 desktop under Window Maker, gnome-terminal focused; x11warp absolute pointer through the guest X server, keyboard ready"
# golden: VM_SIZE 44.9 MiB, baked 2026-09-03 07:47 on the smoke rig from the host-composed tree (scripts/build-guests/tiles/debian22.sh); kernel 2.2.17 booted from the CD prompt with root=/dev/hda1 (no boot loader on the disk), inittab autologin -> X; hdparm -d1 using_dma=1, 66.67 MB/s buffered reads. Restore-proven the same minute: loadvm golden + cont -> desktop in 4 s, XWarpPointer (100,100) and (900,700) read back exactly by XQueryPointer and seen on the framebuffer, keys reach the terminal, second loadvm returns the clean prompt.

# --- POINTER: ABSOLUTE THROUGH THE GUEST'S OWN X SERVER (x11warp) ---
# XFree86 3.3.6 listens on TCP :6000; the launcher forwards 127.0.0.1:6082 ->
# 10.0.2.15:6000 (loopback-only). /etc/X0.hosts in the golden grants 10.0.2.2.
# Buttons and keys ride the QEMU PS/2 path; the sink confirms each warp with
# XQueryPointer before an edge passes. Dead at the console/boot (BackendDown,
# motion dropped, counted) — the loadvm golden always restores a running X.
SH_INPUT_BACKEND=x11warp
SH_X11WARP_DISPLAY=127.0.0.1:82
SH_CURSOR_SCALE=1.0
SH_X11WARP_TRACE=off
